static.solution:
\vec{OP}=\left\lt 0,7,4\right> and \vec{OQ}=\left\lt 3,0,3\right>. Thus,



S=\frac{1}{2} || \vec{OP} \times \vec{OQ} ||



We compute the cross product:



\vec{OP} \times \vec{OQ}=
\left| \begin{array}{ccc}
 \boldsymbol{i} \amp  \boldsymbol{j} \amp  \boldsymbol{k} \\
 0 \amp  7 \amp  4 \\
 3 \amp  0 \amp  3
\end{array} \right|
= 
  \left| \begin{array}{cc} 7 \amp  4 \\ 0 \amp  3 \end{array} \right| \boldsymbol{i}
- \left| \begin{array}{cc} 0 \amp  4 \\ 3 \amp  3 \end{array} \right| \boldsymbol{j}
+ \left| \begin{array}{cc} 0 \amp  7 \\ 3 \amp  0 \end{array} \right| \boldsymbol{k} 


\qquad = 21 \boldsymbol{i} + 12 \boldsymbol{j}  - 21 \boldsymbol{k}



S=\frac{1}{2}|| 21 \boldsymbol{i} + 12 \boldsymbol{j}  - 21 \boldsymbol{k} ||
   =\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{(21)^2+(12)^2+(-21)^2}
   \approx 16.0156.
